      "trading_idea": "Achitouv shows that the return correlation matrix splits cleanly into a few collective 'market modes' (eigenvalues above the rescaled Marchenko-Pastur edge, driven by a handful of high-eigenvector-centrality hubs) and a near-GBM 'noise' bulk, and that the *topology* of the filtered network — local (Onnela-weighted) clustering versus structural-hole position — differs sharply across names. My claim is that what happens next to a purely idiosyncratic shock depends on that topology, not on the shock's size: a name sitting inside a dense, redundant neighbourhood has many substitute instruments through which relative-value desks can immediately hedge and arbitrage a dislocation, so its noise-subspace shock mean-reverts within a minute; a high-degree but low-clustering 'bridge' name has no redundant hedge basket, so market makers widen rather than lean against it and its shock continues as genuine information diffusing between clusters. The trade is therefore a sign-switched residual: short the shock for redundant, densely-clustered names and ride it for bridge names, with the whole signal amplified when the top eigenvalue's variance share (the paper's coupling strength) is elevated, because tight coupling makes idiosyncratic deviations easier to arbitrage. Falsification: if the reversal/continuation coefficient on noise-subspace shocks is statistically indistinguishable across clustering-coefficient terciles once liquidity and volatility are controlled, the mechanism is dead and the factor collapses to plain reversal.",
      "description": "On a rolling window of 10-second log returns, eigendecompose the cross-sectional correlation matrix, define the market subspace as the eigenvalues exceeding the Marchenko-Pastur edge (rescaled by the top eigenvalue), project out that subspace to get each name's noise-subspace residual shock over the last few bars, then multiply the standardized residual by a centered, cross-sectionally ranked weight built from the Onnela-weighted local clustering coefficient (and degree/eigenvector centrality) of the thresholded market-mode graph, so redundant hub-embedded names get a reversal sign and low-clustering bridge names a continuation sign, with the whole signal scaled by the top eigenvalue's explained-variance share.",
      "prediction_horizon": 6,
      "suggested_horizons": [6],
      "source_paper_ids": ["inferring_financial_stock_returns_correlation_from_complex_n"]
